-349288fa8898","position":{"commit_sha":"5cac41af538c6e5c958fa467cb44afa723f5c538","position":"1788576889307894001-05926a8a-94d2-4ca7-8eb9-349288fa8898"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"52053682150a1bcf60cf9a9cb77e71f0f490ddbd9c592d52aad73340787eb77e","event_uuid":"b99364cb-d961-448b-b629-3198416f0462","position":{"commit_sha":"e17b3892144b94baaa7842541bd43ac8a618ef70","position":"1788577254131325001-b99364cb-d961-448b-b629-3198416f0462"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local CLI fallback migrated 4/5 selected per-file tickets to grouped replacements; newly closed=3, already closed=1, errors=1.","timestamp":1788575635713201001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Migration recovery: 51 of 1,499 source tickets were already closed as superseded; the remaining pass is switching from repeated alias scans to a one-time canonical-ID map. Tracker delivery was flushed before resuming.","timestamp":1788576889307894001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Migration checkpoint: 57 source tickets are closed as superseded. Serial administrative-close prechecks are whole-store-bound at this corpus size; profiling is underway before the remaining 1,442 closes.","timestamp":1788577254131325001}],"created_at":1788570271406512725,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe per-file comment-remediation tree under `lettered-depressing-willet` creates excessive planning and coordination overhead. The audited requirements remain valid, but related files should be remediated together without losing file-specific constraints or behavior-bearing consumers.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the per-file tree with subsystem workstreams and bounded directory cohorts. Each leaf group owns a non-overlapping edit set, carries every migrated preserve requirement in its Scope, and records the same paths in file impact. Each group will supersede its source tickets; the old tree is retired only after a one-to-one coverage audit. This fits the work because comment-only edits within one subsystem share review and verification while remaining independently deliverable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every migrated file's comments or docstrings state only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints; verified by the leaf ticket's row-by-row diff review.\n- [ ] Every migrated preserve requirement and behavior-bearing consumer remains explicit and accurate; verified by leaf completion comments and commands.\n- [ ] Every audited path appears in exactly one replacement leaf Scope and exactly one replacement file-impact record; verified by the migration inventory.\n- [ ] Every retired per-file ticket has exactly one live replacement with a net-active `replacement -supersedes-> old` link; verified through the tracker graph.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Production-source workstream: authored package, CLI, MCP, reconciler, and review-bot source.\n- Core unit-test workstream: unit tests outside the reconciler subtree.\n- Reconciler unit-test workstream: reconciler unit cases and fixtures.\n- Other-test workstream: interface, script, integration, external, and end-to-end tests.\n- Developer-tooling workstream: maintainer and analysis scripts.\n- Delivery-infrastructure workstream: CI, Gerrit, deployment, and infrastructure configuration.\n\nEach workstream delegates to disjoint leaf cohorts and applies every acceptance criterion to its own path set.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"This container makes no repository edits directly. Its descendant group tickets hold the exact edit paths; their commits and completion comments are the implementation evidence.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Remediate bloated comments in related file groups","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["441ac84b-a6c6-4cc4-ab1e-3085a13a0206","811a8a6c-0f13-4b98-b3a8-31c227708be3","d959fc4e-916a-487a-a3e4-5cb2a38669ce","05926a8a-94d2-4ca7-8eb9-349288fa8898","b99364cb-d961-448b-b629-3198416f0462"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788577254131325002,"uuid":"c86be009-29df-42a4-b370-721656bcde44"}